{title: Eubulus Sends You Greetings}
{subtitle: 2 Timothy 4:21; 4:6–21; 4:10–21}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Eb] |
| [Ebm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]In the cold Roman [Dm7]cell I wait
[Eb]Winter comes before the [Bb]day is done
The world has turned its [Dm7]face away
[Eb]But I have kept the [Bb]faith [F/A]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Gm]Eubulus sends you greet[Dm7]ings
[Eb]And so do Pudens and Li[Bb]nus [F/A]
[Gm]Claudia and all the broth[Dm7]ers
Greeting you from [Eb]Rome
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Demas has gone to Thessa[Dm7]lonica
[Eb]Crescens has gone to Ga[Bb]latia
Only Luke re[Dm7]mains with me
[Eb]Bring Mark for ser[Bb]vice [F/A]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]At my first defense [Gm]no one stood by me
[Cm7]Everyone a[Gm]bandoned me
[Eb]But the Lord stood [F]by me
[Eb]And gave me strength to [Bb]speak [F/A]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm]Do your best to come before [Dm7]winter
[Eb]Eubulus sends you greetings
{end_of_verse}
